+## 2026-07-24 · Correction — root cause is THIN USAGE, not a single broken feeder
+
+Read `reflection.ts` and checked proposal shapes. My "reflection trigger is the bottleneck" claim was
+over-attributed. Verified facts:
+
+- All 4 proposals are `target_type='work_item'`, `operation='create'`, **`edited_payload` null (edited=0)**.
+- `runReflection` mines ONLY `target_type='work_item'` proposals with `edited_payload` set, clustered ≥2 by
+  changed-field-set. With 0 edits, **triggering reflection today returns `proposalsCreated:0` and mints
+  nothing** (early return before any write). So it would neither validate the engine nor seed the store.
+- There are **two** capture paths, and NEITHER has been exercised:
+  1. **`propose_memory` tool** (`agent/tools.ts:50`, prompted at `runtime.ts:22`) — agent proposes a
+     decision/fact memory only when a user asks to "remember/log" something. **0 `target_type='memory'`
+     proposals have ever been created.**
+  2. **Reflection** (rules from recurring human edits) — never triggered (3ecc1859) AND nothing to mine.
+
+**Corrected root cause:** the store is empty because of **thin/early usage** — the memory plumbing
+(`propose_memory` tool, reflection engine, apply path, injection) is built and appears wired, but the
+activity that produces memories (a user asking to log a decision; humans editing agent proposals) hasn't
+happened in the 7 runs so far. Both a5ecc5aa (ranker) and 3ecc1859 (reflection trigger) are **premature
+until real usage accumulates memories** — 3ecc1859 is a real latent gap, not the current binding reason.
+
+**Implication for validation:** to exercise the pipeline end-to-end, the direct path is `propose_memory`
+(create) → apply → `memories` row → injection — NOT reflection. That writes prod data; needs go-ahead.
